From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [trainer, rollout] feat: score centering on the sampler's
 top-k heads

algorithm.rollout_correction.score_centering (with actor.policy_loss.rollout_correction, bypass-mode REINFORCE):
every response token's policy-gradient term is centered by the expected score under the sampler's top-k head,
sum_H sg[q w - alpha p] log p, where q and p are the sampler's and the trainer's probabilities of the head tokens,
w is the rollout_is weight rule (1 without IS) and alpha = rho w(1/rho) rescales the tail. With truncated IS the
term cancels the truncation's push toward tokens the trainer overestimates; without IS it centers the score under
the sampler.

rollout.topk_log_probs = k makes vLLM return the top-k head of every generated token (flat logprobs, no
detokenization). The agent loops keep one head per response token, with placeholder heads for context tokens
aligned to ContinuousTokenBuilder's edits, and pass them to the trainer through the transfer queue; the FSDP
engine computes the trainer's log-probs at the head ids (train_head_log_probs) in the logits-processor slot, and
the actor loss adds advantages * correction (logged as actor/sc_correction).

The config check accepts fused kernels with fused_kernel_options.impl_backend=torch. The FSDP engine rejects score
centering with fused kernels unless its fused forward returns those log-probs:
FSDPEngineWithLMHead.support_fused_score_centering, False here, is set by an engine subclass that passes the head
ids in and adds the centering term to the model output.
